; Nolang alias catalog: fr
; Display names (别名) and keystroke columns for every std function/method,
; keyed by the same doc anchor its `; [label](#anchor)` comment uses, so an
; alias and its documentation block always agree on the key. One row per
; anchor, as a POSITIONAL array:
;
;   'args.get': ['获取参数', 'g', 'hqcs', 'huoqucanshu']   zh-CN, with pinyin
;   'args.get': ['取得參數', 'g', 'qdhs', 'fm32k6h0gj4']   zh-TW, with zhuyin
;   'args.get': ['Get argument', 'g', 'ga']                every other locale
;
;   [0] alias   display name shown by hover
;   [1] enkeys  initials of the identifier — required, same in every locale
;   [2] keys    initials of the localized name — required
;   [3] full    full keystrokes — optional: pinyin (zh-CN) or zhuyin key
;               positions on a Dachen keyboard (zh-TW). No other locale
;               carries it, so its presence is what marks a Chinese catalog.
;
; The order is a contract, not a convention: a row must have 3 or 4 elements
; and every element must be a string. enkeys and keys are ASCII [a-z0-9];
; full also uses the punctuation keys that carry bopomofo
; (ㄝ=, ㄡ=. ㄤ=; ㄥ=/ ㄦ=-). Completion compares these byte for byte against
; what the editor reports as typed, so a non-ASCII cell would silently never
; match. The identifier itself remains the only spelling that compiles —
; these columns only tell the completion provider which identifier the reader
; is reaching for. Keys must exist as an anchor in some src/std .no source, or
; the gate rejects the catalog; `make i18n -alias-missing` lists what is left.
